        {
          "id": "1776607143072",
          "code": "CHECK_CONTRACT_DOCUMENTS_EMPTY",
          "type": "CODE",
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Check Contract Documents Empty",
            "sourceCode": "const documentsOutput = $context.$nodes.GET_CONTRACT_DOCUMENTS.$output || {};\n\nfunction asArray(value) {\n  if (Array.isArray(value)) {\n    return value;\n  }\n\n  return [];\n}\n\nconst items = asArray(documentsOutput.items);\nconst documentCount = items.length;\nconst hasExistingDocuments = documentCount > 0;\n\nreturn {\n  route: hasExistingDocuments ? 'SKIP_EXISTING' : 'PREVIEW',\n  hasExistingDocuments,\n  documentCount,\n  firstDocument: hasExistingDocuments ? (items[0] || {}) : {}\n};",
            "returnType": "object"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1776607143073"
          },
          "inputs": [],
          "diagram": {
            "x": 5900,
            "y": 6356
          },
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"result\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}"
        },
        {
          "id": "1778000001008",
          "code": "NORMALIZE_UI_QUERY_ROUTER",
          "type": "CODE",
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Normalize UI Query Router",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const routerOutput = ($context.$nodes.ANSWER_OR_ROUTE_QUERY_FROM_UI || {}).$output || {};\nconst parsedContext = (($context.$nodes.PARSE_QUERY_UI_CONTEXT || {}).$output || {}).result || {};\n\nfunction compact(value) {\n  return String(value === null || value === undefined ? '' : value)\n    .replace(/\\s+/g, ' ')\n    .trim();\n}\n\nfunction parseIfJson(value) {\n  if (value && typeof value === 'object' && !Array.isArray(value)) {\n    return value;\n  }\n\n  if (typeof value !== 'string') {\n    return {};\n  }\n\n  const trimmed = value.trim();\n  if (!trimmed) {\n    return {};\n  }\n\n  try {\n    const parsed = JSON.parse(trimmed);\n    return parsed && typeof parsed === 'object' && !Array.isArray(parsed) ? parsed : {};\n  } catch (e) {\n    const fenced = trimmed.match(new RegExp('\\\\x60{3}(?:json)?\\\\s*([\\\\s\\\\S]*?)\\\\x60{3}', 'i'));\n    if (fenced && fenced[1]) {\n      try {\n        const parsedFenced = JSON.parse(fenced[1].trim());\n        return parsedFenced && typeof parsedFenced === 'object' && !Array.isArray(parsedFenced) ? parsedFenced : {};\n      } catch (inner) {\n        return {};\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  return {};\n}\n\nconst normalized = parseIfJson(routerOutput);\nconst visibleContractCount = Number(parsedContext.visibleContractCount || 0);\nconst contractIdCount = Number(parsedContext.contractIdCount || 0);\n\nlet route = compact(normalized.route).toUpperCase();\nif (route !== 'FETCH_CHILD_DATA' && route !== 'ANSWER_FROM_UI_CONTEXT') {\n  route = 'ANSWER_FROM_UI_CONTEXT';\n}\n\nlet childDataNeed = compact(normalized.childDataNeed).toLowerCase();\nif (childDataNeed !== 'deviation_counts' && childDataNeed !== 'clause_details') {\n  childDataNeed = 'none';\n}\n\nlet answer = compact(normalized.answer);\nconst answerLanguage = compact(normalized.answerLanguage) || 'same as user question';\nconst reason = compact(normalized.reason);\n\nif (visibleContractCount === 0) {\n  route = 'ANSWER_FROM_UI_CONTEXT';\n  childDataNeed = 'none';\n  if (!answer) {\n    answer = parsedContext.emptyReason || 'No visible buy or sell contract rows were found in the current workspace.';\n  }\n}\n\nif (route === 'FETCH_CHILD_DATA' && contractIdCount === 0) {\n  route = 'ANSWER_FROM_UI_CONTEXT';\n  childDataNeed = 'none';\n  if (!answer) {\n    answer = 'I can see contract rows, but no contract IDs are available to fetch child clause data.';\n  }\n}\n\nif (route === 'ANSWER_FROM_UI_CONTEXT') {\n  childDataNeed = 'none';\n  if (!answer) {\n    answer = 'I could not determine the answer from the visible contract rows.';\n  }\n}\n\nreturn {\n  route,\n  answer,\n  answerLanguage,\n  childDataNeed,\n  reason,\n  visibleContractCount,\n  contractIdCount\n};"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1778000001002"
          },
          "inputs": [],
          "diagram": {
            "x": 6350,
            "y": 6356
          },
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"result\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "contruct query node",
            "prompt": "You are a deterministic transformer from policy filter strings into Oracle Fusion REST `q` query text.\n\nInputs (exactly 3):\n1) filterStrings = {{$context.$nodes.GET_FILTER_POLICY.$output.filter_strings}}\n2) severityLookup = {{$context.$nodes.GET_SEVERITY_CODE_MEANINGS.$output.result}}\n3) currentDate = {{$context.$system.$currentDateTime}}\n\nOutput JSON (only these keys):\n{\n  \"queryStrings\": [\"(<branch1>)\", \"(<branch2>)\"],\n  \"businessUnitNames\": [\"<BU1>\", \"<BU2>\"],\n  \"orgPlaceholders\": [{\"name\":\"<BU1>\",\"placeholder\":\"__ORG_ID_1__\"}],\n  \"datePlaceholders\": [{\"token\":\"__TODAY_MINUS_10_DAYS__\",\"days\":10}]\n}\n\nOutput contract:\n- `queryStrings` must contain one interpreted query item per input filter string.\n- Keep original input order.\n- Do not join items with OR.\n- Wrap each non-empty item in exactly one outer pair of parentheses.\n- If an input item cannot produce a valid query, return an empty string for that position.\n\nField mapping:\n- Business Unit -> OrgId\n- Contract Type -> ContractTypeName\n- Contract Terms Risk Score -> SeverityCode\n- AssignedDate is the assignee-age field.\n\nCore rules:\n- If `filterStrings` is a JSON string, parse it to an array.\n- Process each filter string independently in original order.\n- Preserve grouping parentheses.\n- Treat AND/OR as logical operators.\n- Do not split literal values containing `and` (example: `Item and Services`).\n\nBusiness Unit placeholders:\n- Never resolve BU names to real IDs.\n- Assign placeholders by first appearance: __ORG_ID_1__, __ORG_ID_2__, ...\n- Reuse placeholder for repeated BU names.\n- Clause format: OrgId = '__ORG_ID_n__'\n- Populate `businessUnitNames` and `orgPlaceholders` accordingly.\n- Preserve the exact case of each Business Unit name as it appears in the source filter string; trim leading/trailing spaces only.\n- Do not lowercase, uppercase, title-case, normalize, translate, or otherwise rewrite Business Unit names in `businessUnitNames` or `orgPlaceholders[].name`.\n\nSeverity conversion:\n- Map risk meanings to `LookupCode` using `severityLookup`.\n- Match case-insensitively; ignore spaces, underscores, hyphens.\n- If a severity token is unknown, skip only that token.\n\nClause conversions:\n- `Business Unit is X` -> `OrgId = '__ORG_ID_n__'`\n- `Contract Type is X` -> `ContractTypeName = 'X'`\n- `Contract Terms Risk Score is X` -> `SeverityCode = '<LookupCode>'`\n\nIN preference:\n- For same-field multi-value OR, use `IN`.\n- `Contract Type is (A OR B OR C)` -> `(ContractTypeName in ('A','B','C'))`\n- `Contract Terms Risk Score is (Critical OR High Risk)` -> `(SeverityCode in ('4_CRITICAL','3_HIGH_RISK'))`\n- Deduplicate IN-list values in first-seen order.\n- If one value remains, use `=`.\n\nAssignedDate handling (generic):\n- AssignedDate must never be a future date. Never generate __TODAY_PLUS_* tokens.\n- If user asks for a future-date window for AssignedDate, skip only that date fragment.\n- `more than|older than|at least N days` -> `AssignedDate <= '__TODAY_MINUS_N_DAYS__'`\n- `less than|within|last|past|recent N days` -> `AssignedDate >= '__TODAY_MINUS_N_DAYS__'`\n- `exactly N days ago` -> `AssignedDate = '__TODAY_MINUS_N_DAYS__'`\n- `today` -> `AssignedDate = '__TODAY_MINUS_0_DAYS__'`\n- `yesterday` -> `AssignedDate = '__TODAY_MINUS_1_DAYS__'`\n- `between X and Y days ago` -> let older=max(X,Y), newer=min(X,Y), then use `(AssignedDate >= '__TODAY_MINUS_<older>_DAYS__' and AssignedDate <= '__TODAY_MINUS_<newer>_DAYS__')` (example: X=10,Y=30 -> `AssignedDate >= '__TODAY_MINUS_30_DAYS__' and AssignedDate <= '__TODAY_MINUS_10_DAYS__'`)\n- `before <YYYY-MM-DD>` -> `AssignedDate < 'YYYY-MM-DD'`\n- `on or before <YYYY-MM-DD>` -> `AssignedDate <= 'YYYY-MM-DD'`\n- `after <YYYY-MM-DD>` -> `AssignedDate > 'YYYY-MM-DD'`\n- `on or after <YYYY-MM-DD>` -> `AssignedDate >= 'YYYY-MM-DD'`\n- If date intent is ambiguous (example: \"old contracts\" with no threshold/date), do not invent a value; skip only that date fragment.\n\nDate placeholders:\n- Collect unique `__TODAY_MINUS_N_DAYS__` tokens used across all `queryStrings`.\n- Populate `datePlaceholders` as `{token, days}`.\n\nStrict output:\n- Return strict JSON only.\n- No markdown, no explanation, no extra keys.\nQuoted literal handling:\n- Treat single-quoted values as literal boundaries. Logical operators inside quoted values are part of the value, not AND/OR operators.\n- Do not split `AND` or `OR` when they appear inside a quoted Business Unit or Contract Type value.\n- Preserve parentheses, commas, hyphens, underscores, and doubled apostrophes inside quoted values.\n- Preserve doubled apostrophes exactly as provided, e.g. `Children''s Services` remains `Children''s Services`.\n- Trim only outside whitespace around the complete quoted value; do not trim or normalize inside the value.\n- `Contract Type is 'Items AND Services Procurement'` -> `ContractTypeName = 'Items AND Services Procurement'`\n- `Contract Type is 'Children''s Services (Global)'` -> `ContractTypeName = 'Children''s Services (Global)'`\n- `Contract Type is ('Children''s Services (Global)' OR 'Items AND Services Procurement')` -> `ContractTypeName in ('Children''s Services (Global)','Items AND Services Procurement')`\n- `Business Unit is 'Items AND Services Procurement'` -> `OrgId = '__ORG_ID_n__'` and `businessUnitNames` contains `Items AND Services Procurement`.\n- When values are not quoted, still avoid splitting `AND` or `OR` inside a Business Unit or Contract Type value unless the text after the operator starts a new supported field clause such as Business Unit, Contract Type, Contract Terms Risk Score, or AssignedDate.\n\nADF datetime handling for AssignedDate:\n- AssignedDate is an Oracle ADF REST datetime field, not a date-only field.\n- For relative date requests, keep using placeholders such as '__TODAY_MINUS_10_DAYS__'; do not emit final date or datetime literals directly for relative dates.\n- BUILD_REST_QUERY is responsible for resolving date placeholders to ADF datetime literals in the format YYYY-MM-DDT00:00:00.000+00:00.\n- If an explicit YYYY-MM-DD date appears in a policy filter for AssignedDate, keep the date in YYYY-MM-DD order; BUILD_REST_QUERY will normalize AssignedDate date-only literals to ADF datetime literals.\n"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1776607143066"
          },
          "code": "CONTRUCT_QUERY_NODE",
