        {
          "id": "1776607143074",
          "code": "BUILD_PREVIEW_CONFIRMATION_CONTEXT",
          "type": "CODE",
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Build Preview Confirmation Context",
            "sourceCode": "const actionContext = (($context.$nodes.PARSE_PREVIEW_ACTION_CONTEXT.$output || {}).result) || {};\nconst documentCheck = (($context.$nodes.CHECK_CONTRACT_DOCUMENTS_EMPTY.$output || {}).result) || {};\nconst previewNode = (($context.$nodes || {}).PREVIEW_AND_ATTACH_CONTRACT || {});\nconst previewOutput = previewNode.$output || {};\n\nfunction compact(value) {\n  return String(value || '').trim();\n}\n\nconst contractId = compact(actionContext.contractId);\nconst documentCount = Number(documentCheck.documentCount || 0);\nconst previewRequested = documentCheck.route === 'PREVIEW';\nconst action = previewRequested ? 'PreviewGenerated' : 'PreviewSkippedExistingDocument';\nconst message = previewRequested\n  ? 'Preview and attach was requested for contract ' + contractId + '.'\n  : 'A contract document already exists for contract ' + contractId + ', so preview generation was skipped.';\n\nreturn {\n  action,\n  contractId,\n  previewRequested,\n  skippedBecauseExistingDocument: !previewRequested,\n  documentCount,\n  existingDocument: documentCheck.firstDocument || {},\n  previewAndAttachResult: previewOutput,\n  message\n};",
            "returnType": "object"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "14"
          },
          "inputs": [],
          "diagram": {
            "x": 5450,
            "y": 7022
          },
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"result\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MULTIRECORD"
              ],
              "customNotes": "Use one Multi Record widget. patternId must be exactly \"multiRecordWidget\". Set title to an empty string. Use properties.cols and properties.rows only; do not add description, subtitle, properties.subtitle, or properties.summary. Use ContractNumber in summaries, never ContractId. Columns must be Contract, Description, Supplier, Assignee, Severity, and Assigned Since. The Supplier column value must come from PartyName. Count severity using lookup codes: 4_CRITICAL for critical and 3_HIGH_RISK for high-risk. Severity cells must be badge objects, not quoted JSON strings. Keep Contract drilldown with intent buy. Use DATA.items[].SeverityPriority exactly; do not recalculate severity badge priority from text or lookup meanings. Supplier column and drilldown behavior stay unchanged. Each multiRecord row must be an object with exactly 6 cells matching the columns; Severity appears only as the fifth badge cell, never as extra duplicate string cells."
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "show contracts list",
            "prompt": "Generate a procurement contract list display using DATA.\n\nDATA: {{$context.$nodes.NORMALIZE_CONTRACT_FIELDS_FROM_BATCH.$output.result.listData}}\n\nOUTPUT REQUIREMENTS:\n1. First output one plain-text summary sentence.\n2. Then output exactly one raw <oraInfoDisplay key=\"list\"> block containing one complete valid JSON object for `multiRecordWidget`.\n3. Do not output markdown fences, quotes, CDATA, explanatory prose, raw instructions, source DATA, or extra text before the summary, between the summary and block, or after the block.\n4. Escape quotation marks inside string values and command strings so the JSON remains valid.\n\nSUMMARY RULES:\n- Use DATA.summary.topContracts as the already-counted and already-ranked source for the summary sentence.\n- Do not calculate counts or rank contracts from DATA.items.\n- Mention up to three contractNumber values from DATA.summary.topContracts, in the same order. Never use ContractId, internal ids, or long numeric identifiers.\n- If DATA.summary.hasOpenCriticalOrHighRisk is false, say exactly: No open critical or high-risk requests were found in any contracts.\n- If DATA.summary.hasOpenCritical is true, say the named contracts have the highest volume of open critical requested changes.\n- If DATA.summary.hasOpenCritical is false and DATA.summary.hasOpenHighRisk is true, say the named contracts have the highest volume of open high-risk requested changes.\n- Include open critical counts from DATA.summary.topContracts only when it makes the sentence clearer.\n- Include open high-risk counts from DATA.summary.topContracts only when DATA.summary.hasOpenHighRisk is true.\n- If DATA.summary.hasOpenHighRisk is false, do not use the words high-risk in the summary sentence except inside the exact no-results sentence.\n- If DATA.summary.hasOpenCritical and DATA.summary.hasOpenHighRisk are both true, you may add: along with additional open high-risk requested changes across multiple contracts.\n- Use singular Contract when exactly one contract is named; otherwise use Contracts.\n- Do not mention reviewed, closed, medium-risk, low-risk, or no-risk requests.\n- Use requested change or requested changes; never use deviation or deviations.\n- Do not start with \"Top contracts\" or \"Open critical or high-risk requests are concentrated\".\n- Example when critical and high-risk requests exist: Contracts SLSA_MFG_Test1, RiskScoreContract2518, and RiskScoreContract47 have the highest volume of open critical requested changes, along with additional open high-risk requested changes across multiple contracts.\n- Example when only critical requests exist: Contracts NDA 100, ISP-091001-25S, and ISP-140526-25R have the highest volume of open critical requested changes.\n- The only-critical example is the required style whenever DATA.summary.hasOpenHighRisk is false.\n\nMULTI RECORD JSON RULES:\n- Use this shape:\n  {\n    \"title\": \"\",\n    \"patternId\": \"multiRecordWidget\",\n    \"properties\": {\n      \"cols\": [\"Contract\", \"Description\", \"Supplier\", \"Assignee\", \"Severity\", \"Assigned Since\"],\n      \"rows\": [ ... ]\n    }\n  }\n- The widget title must be an empty string. Do not add any other title, description, subtitle, properties.subtitle, or properties.summary.\n- Use the local wrapper shape exactly: top-level `title`, `patternId`, and `properties`; do not use `config`.\n- Use one row per DATA.items item in source order. rows.length must equal DATA.items.length.\n- Each row must be a JSON object with a `cells` array and optional `drillDownAction`; never output a raw cells array.\n- Row cells, in order:\n  1. ContractNumber\n  2. Description or empty string\n  3. PartyName or empty string\n  4. Assignee or empty string\n  5. { \"type\": \"badge\", \"text\": DATA.items[].SeverityBadgeText or \"\", \"priority\": DATA.items[].SeverityPriority or \"neutral\" }\n  6. AssignedDate formatted MM/DD/YYYY, or empty string\n- Each row.cells array must contain exactly 6 entries, matching the 6 columns in order; do not append any extra cells after Assigned Since.\n- The Severity cell must be a JSON object, not a quoted JSON string.\n- Valid Severity cell example: { \"type\": \"badge\", \"text\": \"Critical\", \"priority\": \"alert\" }\n- Invalid Severity cell example: \"{\\\"type\\\":\\\"badge\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Critical\\\",\\\"priority\\\":\\\"alert\\\"}\"\n- DATA.items[].SeverityPriority is already prepared upstream; copy it exactly for the Severity badge priority, do not derive it from severity text or lookup code, and use \"neutral\" only when it is missing or empty.\n- The Severity value may appear only as the fifth cell badge object; do not output SeverityBadgeText, SeverityCode, or SeverityPriority as standalone string cells or duplicate severity cells.\n- Valid Severity badge priority values are: \"alert\", \"warning\", \"medium\", \"neutral\", \"success\".\n- Never show lookup codes such as 4_CRITICAL, 3_HIGH_RISK, 2_MEDIUM_RISK, 1_LOW_RISK, or 0_NO_RISK.\n- Add drillDownAction for rows with ContractId using: ora.Invoke('Drilldown', '{\"contractId\":\"<ContractId>\",\"intent\":\"<DATA.intent>\"}')\n- Replace <DATA.intent> with DATA.intent exactly. Drilldown payload must contain only contractId and intent."
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "SHOW_CONTRACTS_LIST",
          "id": "1776443362436",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1776443362436_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Generate a procurement contract list display using DATA.\n\nDATA: {{$context.$nodes.NORMALIZE_CONTRACT_FIELDS_FROM_BATCH.$output.result.listData}}\n\nOUTPUT REQUIREMENTS:\n1. First output one plain-text summary sentence.\n2. Then output exactly one raw <oraInfoDisplay key=\"list\"> block containing one complete valid JSON object for `multiRecordWidget`.\n3. Do not output markdown fences, quotes, CDATA, explanatory prose, raw instructions, source DATA, or extra text before the summary, between the summary and block, or after the block.\n4. Escape quotation marks inside string values and command strings so the JSON remains valid.\n\nSUMMARY RULES:\n- Use DATA.summary.topContracts as the already-counted and already-ranked source for the summary sentence.\n- Do not calculate counts or rank contracts from DATA.items.\n- Mention up to three contractNumber values from DATA.summary.topContracts, in the same order. Never use ContractId, internal ids, or long numeric identifiers.\n- If DATA.summary.hasOpenCriticalOrHighRisk is false, say exactly: No open critical or high-risk requests were found in any contracts.\n- If DATA.summary.hasOpenCritical is true, say the named contracts have the highest volume of open critical requested changes.\n- If DATA.summary.hasOpenCritical is false and DATA.summary.hasOpenHighRisk is true, say the named contracts have the highest volume of open high-risk requested changes.\n- Include open critical counts from DATA.summary.topContracts only when it makes the sentence clearer.\n- Include open high-risk counts from DATA.summary.topContracts only when DATA.summary.hasOpenHighRisk is true.\n- If DATA.summary.hasOpenHighRisk is false, do not use the words high-risk in the summary sentence except inside the exact no-results sentence.\n- If DATA.summary.hasOpenCritical and DATA.summary.hasOpenHighRisk are both true, you may add: along with additional open high-risk requested changes across multiple contracts.\n- Use singular Contract when exactly one contract is named; otherwise use Contracts.\n- Do not mention reviewed, closed, medium-risk, low-risk, or no-risk requests.\n- Use requested change or requested changes; never use deviation or deviations.\n- Do not start with \"Top contracts\" or \"Open critical or high-risk requests are concentrated\".\n- Example when critical and high-risk requests exist: Contracts SLSA_MFG_Test1, RiskScoreContract2518, and RiskScoreContract47 have the highest volume of open critical requested changes, along with additional open high-risk requested changes across multiple contracts.\n- Example when only critical requests exist: Contracts NDA 100, ISP-091001-25S, and ISP-140526-25R have the highest volume of open critical requested changes.\n- The only-critical example is the required style whenever DATA.summary.hasOpenHighRisk is false.\n\nMULTI RECORD JSON RULES:\n- Use this shape:\n  {\n    \"title\": \"\",\n    \"patternId\": \"multiRecordWidget\",\n    \"properties\": {\n      \"cols\": [\"Contract\", \"Description\", \"Supplier\", \"Assignee\", \"Severity\", \"Assigned Since\"],\n      \"rows\": [ ... ]\n    }\n  }\n- The widget title must be an empty string. Do not add any other title, description, subtitle, properties.subtitle, or properties.summary.\n- Use the local wrapper shape exactly: top-level `title`, `patternId`, and `properties`; do not use `config`.\n- Use one row per DATA.items item in source order. rows.length must equal DATA.items.length.\n- Each row must be a JSON object with a `cells` array and optional `drillDownAction`; never output a raw cells array.\n- Row cells, in order:\n  1. ContractNumber\n  2. Description or empty string\n  3. PartyName or empty string\n  4. Assignee or empty string\n  5. { \"type\": \"badge\", \"text\": DATA.items[].SeverityBadgeText or \"\", \"priority\": DATA.items[].SeverityPriority or \"neutral\" }\n  6. AssignedDate formatted MM/DD/YYYY, or empty string\n- Each row.cells array must contain exactly 6 entries, matching the 6 columns in order; do not append any extra cells after Assigned Since.\n- The Severity cell must be a JSON object, not a quoted JSON string.\n- Valid Severity cell example: { \"type\": \"badge\", \"text\": \"Critical\", \"priority\": \"alert\" }\n- Invalid Severity cell example: \"{\\\"type\\\":\\\"badge\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Critical\\\",\\\"priority\\\":\\\"alert\\\"}\"\n- DATA.items[].SeverityPriority is already prepared upstream; copy it exactly for the Severity badge priority, do not derive it from severity text or lookup code, and use \"neutral\" only when it is missing or empty.\n- The Severity value may appear only as the fifth cell badge object; do not output SeverityBadgeText, SeverityCode, or SeverityPriority as standalone string cells or duplicate severity cells.\n- Valid Severity badge priority values are: \"alert\", \"warning\", \"medium\", \"neutral\", \"success\".\n- Never show lookup codes such as 4_CRITICAL, 3_HIGH_RISK, 2_MEDIUM_RISK, 1_LOW_RISK, or 0_NO_RISK.\n- Add drillDownAction for rows with ContractId using: ora.Invoke('Drilldown', '{\"contractId\":\"<ContractId>\",\"intent\":\"<DATA.intent>\"}')\n- Replace <DATA.intent> with DATA.intent exactly. Drilldown payload must contain only contractId and intent."
            },
            {
              "id": "1776443362436_systemPrompt",
              "name": "systemPrompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You output strict multiRecordWidget info display for the Contracts Compliance Workspace. Use only DATA; do not invent contract names, counts, severities, dates, assignees, or drilldown payload fields. The plain text before the widget is the only panel summary."
