          "metadata": {
            "name": "Summary Contracts",
            "prompt": "You are generating the Summary stage response for contract negotiation monitoring.\n\nDATA:\n{{$context.$nodes.NORMALIZE_CONTRACT_FIELDS_FROM_BATCH.$output.result.summaryData}}\n\nTASK:\nReturn valid Markdown with a fixed headline and one business summary sentence based on DATA.summary.\n\nDATA USE RULES:\n- Use DATA.summary.topContracts as the already-counted and already-ranked source for top contracts.\n- Do not calculate counts or rank contracts from DATA.items. DATA.items is intentionally not provided.\n- If DATA.summary.hasOpenCriticalOrHighRisk is false, line 3 must say no open critical or high-risk requests were found.\n- Mention up to three contractNumber values from DATA.summary.topContracts, in the same order.\n- Use openCriticalCount and openHighRiskCount from DATA.summary.topContracts for any contract counts.\n- Do not lead with aggregate totals such as total requested-change count.\n- Use aggregate totals only if they are needed to make the summary more actionable.\n- Omit count phrases whose value is 0.\n- Do not mention reviewed, closed, medium-risk, low-risk, or no-risk requests.\n- Never invent counts or contract numbers.\n\nSTYLE RULES:\n- Line 3 must be natural, conversational business language.\n- Do not print raw counter keys such as openCriticalCount or openHighRiskCount.\n- Use readable phrases like open critical requested changes and open high-risk requested changes.\n- Keep line 3 crisp, factual, and focused on the contracts requiring attention.\n- Example style: NDA 100 leads with 5 open critical requested changes, followed by ISP-091001-25S and ISP-140526-25R with 4 open critical requested changes each.\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT (STRICT):\n- Line 1 must be exactly: # Contracts under negotiation with critical and high-risk requests require immediate attention.\n- Line 2 must be blank.\n- Line 3 must be exactly one sentence.\n- Do not repeat heading words in line 3.\n- Never use the words deviation or deviations; use requested change or requested changes.\n- No bullets.\n- No numbering.\n- No extra lines.\n\nIf data is empty, output exactly:\n# Contracts under negotiation with critical and high-risk requests require immediate attention.\n\nNo matching contracts were found."
          },
