          "id": "1778000001006",
          "code": "ANSWER_QUERY_FROM_UI_CONTEXT",
          "type": "LLM",
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Answer Query From UI Context",
            "prompt": "DATA:\n{{$context.$nodes.BUILD_QUERY_ANSWER_CONTEXT.$output.result}}\n\nUSER QUESTION:\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\nTASK:\nAnswer the user question using only DATA. DATA contains visible contract rows plus compact computed child deviation/requested-change data fetched only because the router determined child data was needed.\n\nRules:\n- Return concise plain text only.\n- Answer in DATA.answerLanguage / the same language as the user question.\n- Lead with the direct insight.\n- Prefer one short sentence when possible.\n- Include only fields needed to answer the question.\n- For count, group, rank, comparison, highest, maximum, largest, top, or \"most\" questions, use deviationCount, deviationCounters, maxDeviationCount, and maxDeviationContracts, and give the top result with its count.\n- If DATA.answerHint is non-empty and the question asks which contract has the most/highest/maximum/largest number of deviations/requested changes/clauses, use DATA.answerHint as the factual basis, translated to the user's language if needed.\n- For list questions, provide the relevant list concisely and completely when the question calls for a list.\n- For clause detail questions, use DATA.contracts[].deviations only when present and summarize the relevant clauses/issues briefly.\n- Avoid verbose explanations, raw JSON, markdown tables, widgets, code fences, row-by-row detail, and process commentary.\n- Do not guess from top-level severity.\n- Mention the panel only when it helps disambiguate buy/procurement versus sell/sales rows.\n- If the answer cannot be determined from DATA, say so clearly and do not invent missing details."
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "inputs": [
